From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: select caption glyphs by the content rectangle

Purpose: draw the XP-sized glyphs on Luna caption buttons. The Window
CloseButton/MinButton/MaxButton parts select their glyph image by size
and provide glyphs of 9, 13, 19 and 23 pixels. Wine compared the outer
21x21 button with each glyph and chose 19x19, so the cross, bar and box
looked too large. XP uses the 13x13 glyph at that size, which matches
choosing and centring inside the 2px content margins (17x17). At 144
and 192 DPI the 32 and 42 pixel buttons still select the 23x23 glyph.
Limited to the opted-in external shell. The pixels of an active close
button now match the reference XP screen. No Microsoft binary is
changed and no theme resource is exported.

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c b/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c
index 35d138d..2f523f9 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c
@@ -617,6 +617,21 @@ static HRESULT UXTHEME_DrawImageGlyph(HTHEME hTheme, HDC hdc, int iPartId,
     POINT srcSize;
     POINT topleft;
     BOOL hasAlpha, hasDefaultTransparentColour;
+    RECT content;
+    MARGINS margins;
+
+    /* XP chooses and centres size-selected glyphs inside the content rectangle.
+     * A 21x21 Luna caption button has 2px content margins and uses its 13x13
+     * glyph; choosing by the outer rectangle selected the 19x19 glyph. */
+    if (GetEnvironmentVariableW(L"WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL", NULL, 0) &&
+        SUCCEEDED(GetThemeMargins(hTheme, hdc, iPartId, iStateId, TMT_CONTENTMARGINS, NULL, &margins)))
+    {
+        content.left = pRect->left + margins.cxLeftWidth;
+        content.top = pRect->top + margins.cyTopHeight;
+        content.right = pRect->right - margins.cxRightWidth;
+        content.bottom = pRect->bottom - margins.cyBottomHeight;
+        if (content.right > content.left && content.bottom > content.top) pRect = &content;
+    }
 
     hr = UXTHEME_LoadImage(hTheme, iPartId, iStateId, pRect, TRUE, &bmpSrc, &rcSrc, &hasAlpha,
                            &hasDefaultTransparentColour, NULL);
